WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:08.320
We now have a new poll about Americans view&nbsp;
on the proposed but still not passed covid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:13.680
relief bill of Joe Biden. And Democrats will&nbsp;
be speaking to Democratic Congressman Roxana&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.360
a little bit later today. And I'm going to ask him&nbsp;
what's going on and how quickly does he think this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:24.560
is going to move forward. But there is a new&nbsp;
Politico morning consult poll which shows that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:32.960
76 percent of all Americans strongly support or&nbsp;
somewhat support the covid-19 relief bill. This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:38.240
the one point nine trillion dollar bill, not that&nbsp;
tiny six hundred billion dollar package that some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:45.840
Republicans propose. This is the big boy. Only 17&nbsp;
percent of Americans somewhat oppose or strongly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.200
oppose the package. The rest don't even have to&nbsp;
have no opinion at this point. And stunningly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.840 --> 00:01:00.480
among Republicans, 60 percent of Republican&nbsp;
voters strongly or somewhat support the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:07.440
one point nine trillion dollar covid relief&nbsp;
package. This is a really big deal because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.360
in the United Way, it's a big deal for&nbsp;
a bunch of different reasons. No. One,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.320
in the United States over the last eight to&nbsp;
10 years, the level of political division&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:22.240
and polarization makes it really difficult to&nbsp;
ever have more than 50 or 60 percent support&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.720
for almost anything. After the Sandy Hook&nbsp;
shooting during Barack Obama's presidency,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:33.280
there was something like 80, 80 or 90 percent&nbsp;
support for universal background checks for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:39.520
firearm transactions of all kinds. This means&nbsp;
eliminating. Every mechanism by which you could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:46.080
obtain a firearm without a background check, 88,&nbsp;
90 percent support, and it still didn't pass.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.960
And if you hadn't been paying attention to this&nbsp;
reality up until then, it was another reminder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:56.000
that our elected officials are not actually&nbsp;
representing the views of their constituents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.880
because if they were with 80 to 90 percent support&nbsp;
for that, it would have passed. We now are seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.800
essentially every Republican, although&nbsp;
I believe if it comes down to it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:12.160
some Republicans will vote for the covid-19 relief&nbsp;
bill proposed at one point nine trillion dollars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.800
because some pragmatic Republicans recognize that&nbsp;
their constituents want it. But at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:22.640
you have 76 percent of the country saying&nbsp;
we want this passed this it's been proposed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.560
It's been voted on in the House. Joe Biden&nbsp;
wants it. Democrats want it. Presumably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.520
it would pass the Senate with 50 at minimum, 50&nbsp;
votes. And Kamala Harris is the tie breaking vote.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:38.560
And yet we aren't seeing any Republicans come out&nbsp;
and say this is popular with the American people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:44.800
and it's my responsibility to represent them. 76&nbsp;
percent support and even 60 percent of Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:51.840
supporting this and not a single Republican for&nbsp;
now has said, let's do this, I want to vote for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:58.880
this. So, as I've said before, let them vote&nbsp;
it down. Democrats should be spinning this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:07.600
accurately as this has bipartisan support. We're&nbsp;
not talking about Republican senators who are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:13.520
against it. We're talking about with the people.&nbsp;
Seventy six percent of the country, 60 percent of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:19.760
Republicans support this. There is rarely anything&nbsp;
as bipartisan when it comes to public support&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:27.040
as this, where our Republican elected officials on&nbsp;
it pass it via budget reconciliation or attempt to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:33.520
let every single Republican who is committed&nbsp;
to voting against it do it, pass it via budget&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.080
reconciliation. You know, you have the votes with&nbsp;
fifty. Joe Manchin said he supports it. As far as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.760
I last saw, that was about a week ago. Kamala&nbsp;
Harris would be the tie breaking vote, have Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.120
Biden sign it. And if every Republican really&nbsp;
feels confident that they can vote against this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:53.840
without suffering with their own constituents,&nbsp;
let them do it. I don't understand who it is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:58.640
Republican elected officials are representing by&nbsp;
opposing this. Certainly not their constituents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.840
are they? I mean, you know, where we typically&nbsp;
go is are they representing corporate interests?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:09.040
Are they representing donor interests? Are&nbsp;
they representing lobbyists interests? I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:17.600
don't exactly know. But we know that certain&nbsp;
staking out certain positions for Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:21.200
is very lucrative in terms of fundraising.&nbsp;
And maybe that's all that this is. I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.880
know the answer. We'll talk to Roxana&nbsp;
about it a little bit later today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.120
but it's time to do it. It's&nbsp;
it's just time to get it passed.&nbsp;

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:34.800
If you can think of any reason why Democrats&nbsp;
at this point should not go forward with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.640
the one point nine trillion dollar covid&nbsp;
relief bill through budget reconciliation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.640 --> 00:05:54.302
requiring only a simple majority. Let me know.
